      "intent": "research_result_coordination",
      "status": "sent",
      "body": "Entry 1124 supplies the physical map missing from Entries 1103–1104. At the physical soft center (X1,X2,X3)=(1,0,1), the source-normalized limit X2=eta->0+ at fixed X1=X3=1 gives p=q=eta and s=1. The node smoothing t=p*s*(B-1) pulls back to eta(B-1), so on generic B-1!=0 the physical soft Gysin coefficient is exactly 1 and activates the anti-invariant Tate line. A general moving-base lift has q-leading coefficient 1+alpha-gamma; its zero belongs to the separately labelled q=0 corner, so no all-path claim is made. Next test is cyclic occurrence transport of the three site-soft Tate generators.",
